cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Defense Budget Lab, FY2026 and FY2027"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Agard
    given-names: "Alyssa I."
    email: economics@alyssaagard.dev
    website: "https://alyssaagard.dev"
abstract: >-
  An interactive reading of Congressional Research Service reports R48860 and
  R49023 on funding for selected weapon systems, joined line by line across
  fiscal years 2026 and 2027, together with a model of the burdened cost of
  military basic pay and a construction of regular military compensation built
  on the published 2023 compensation tables and the M-1 budget exhibits. The
  work comprises a verified 27 sheet workbook, a generator that reads it, and a
  self contained page that presents it.
keywords:
  - defense budget
  - defense policy
  - appropriations
  - authorization
  - weapon systems
  - military compensation
  - Congressional Research Service
  - reproducible research
